API-06: apply the API external buildup as a rate per day and read it back as set

swmm_SUBCATCH_EXTERNAL_POLLUTANT_BUILDUP was added to the surface at every
runoff step as value x area, with no time-step factor and without being
cleared, so one call produced a buildup proportional to the number of runoff
steps (24 lb/ac with a 1 h DRY_STEP, 288 lb/ac with 5 min, for a value of 1).
surfqual_applyAPIBuildup() now receives the runoff step and adds
value x area x tStep / 86400, i.e. the property is a buildup rate in mass (or
count) per acre or hectare per day, which persists until it is changed like
the node and link mass fluxes. The getter divided the stored value by
UCF(LANDAREA) (43,560x in US units) although the setter stores it unscaled;
it now returns the value as set.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply API-06_swmm530.patch

